# Implementation Plan - Project-wide Font Size Correction

Improve readability and visual hierarchy across the entire app by scaling up too-small font configurations and overriding arbitrary micro-pixel class definitions.

## Proposed Changes

### Frontend Styles & Theme

---

#### [MODIFY] [tailwind.config.js](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/frontend/tailwind.config.js)
- Extend standard text utility mappings in Tailwind's `fontSize` to scale up standard styles:
  - `xs`: Scale from default `0.75rem` (12px) to `0.8125rem` (13px)
  - `sm`: Scale from default `0.875rem` (14px) to `0.9375rem` (15px)
  - `base`: Scale from default `1rem` (16px) to `1.0625rem` (17px)
  - `lg`: Scale from default `1.125rem` (18px) to `1.1875rem` (19px)
  - `xl`: Scale from default `1.25rem` (20px) to `1.375rem` (22px)

#### [MODIFY] [index.css](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/frontend/src/index.css)
- Set base `html` font size to `103.125%` or `16.5px` to slightly scale up all `rem` metrics.
- Implement explicit overrides for Tailwind's arbitrary pixel selectors (like `.text-\[9px\]` and `.text-\[10px\]`) to map them to more legible font-sizes (e.g. `11px` and `12.5px`).

